1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,334
WenQuest's assessment system is built for university audits,

2
00:00:03,354 --> 00:00:05,807
program accreditation and internal teaching reviews.

3
00:00:06,827 --> 00:00:11,077
Every step a student takes leaves evidence: diagnosis and practice,

4
00:00:11,547 --> 00:00:12,668
virtual labs,

5
00:00:13,138 --> 00:00:14,897
exams, and an AI defense panel.

6
00:00:15,917 --> 00:00:19,653
A transcript is more than a grade: it carries an ability profile,

7
00:00:20,123 --> 00:00:22,516
and every score traces back to evidence.

8
00:00:23,536 --> 00:00:26,985
Teachers handle only the cases that need human judgement.

9
00:00:28,005 --> 00:00:30,943
This student scored 86 on the closed-book exam,

10
00:00:30,963 --> 00:00:34,531
but the lab log shows a first-try hit with no prediction.

11
00:00:35,001 --> 00:00:36,930
The system schedules an oral exam;

12
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:39,359
the AI does not call it cheating.

13
00:00:40,379 --> 00:00:44,062
The school gets a course-objective attainment report in one click,

14
00:00:44,532 --> 00:00:46,271
and a teaching-quality report.

15
00:00:47,291 --> 00:00:49,131
They come on the web and in Word,

16
00:00:49,601 --> 00:00:53,750
with improvement actions drafted by AI and confirmed by teachers.

17
00:00:54,770 --> 00:00:58,652
The Campus Hub rolls courses up to each program's graduate attributes,

18
00:00:59,122 --> 00:01:01,555
and flags any indicator that falls short.

19
00:01:02,575 --> 00:01:06,307
Click through to the course and the assessment item that is holding it back.

20
00:01:07,327 --> 00:01:09,763
Assign an improvement task in one click,

21
00:01:10,233 --> 00:01:13,790
and re-check it next term: evaluate, feed back, improve.

22
00:01:14,810 --> 00:01:19,099
The demo uses simulated data. Schools are welcome to pilot it.
